Subject: [PATCH] Stop waiting on an initializing parent package in importlib

The 3.13 backport of gh-130094 (python/cpython#155915), first released
in 3.13.16 and still present in 3.13.17, makes _find_and_load_unlocked()
re-import a parent package that is still initializing while it holds the
submodule's module lock. When one thread runs pkg/__init__.py (holding
pkg's lock) and that file imports pkg.sub, while a second thread imports
pkg.sub directly, each thread waits on the other's lock and importlib
raises _DeadlockError. The Agent imports Python checks from several
goroutines, so some checks fail to load at startup.

Remove that block to restore the 3.13.15 behavior. The rest of the
backport (copying sys.meta_path before iterating it) is kept.
Reported upstream as python/cpython#160045; drop this patch once a
3.13 release fixes it.
---
 Lib/importlib/_bootstrap.py | 6 ------
 1 file changed, 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Lib/importlib/_bootstrap.py b/Lib/importlib/_bootstrap.py
--- a/Lib/importlib/_bootstrap.py
+++ b/Lib/importlib/_bootstrap.py
@@ -1321,12 +1321,6 @@
             msg = f'{_ERR_MSG_PREFIX}{name!r}; {parent!r} is not a package'
             raise ModuleNotFoundError(msg, name=name) from None
         parent_spec = parent_module.__spec__
-        if getattr(parent_spec, '_initializing', False):
-            _call_with_frames_removed(import_, parent)
-        # Crazy side-effects (again)!
-        module = sys.modules.get(name)
-        if module is not None:
-            return module
         child = name.rpartition('.')[2]
     spec = _find_spec(name, path)
     if spec is None:
